@startuml
!include theme.iuml
title Record and Stage Microphone Audio
hide footbox
autonumber
actor Contributor
participant "app : App" as App
participant "recorder : Recorder" as Recorder
participant "audio_utils\n<<module>>" as Audio

note over App, Recorder
  Precondition: optional imports succeeded, recorder exists,
  and the microphone can be opened. Recording is initially off.
end note
activate Contributor
Contributor -> App : toggle_recording() (Record)
activate App
App -> Recorder : start()
activate Recorder
create participant "stream : InputStream" as Stream
Recorder -> Stream : InputStream(44100 Hz, mono, callback)
activate Stream
Stream --> Recorder : Stream instance
deactivate Stream
Recorder -> Stream : start()
activate Stream
Stream --> Recorder : Capture started
deactivate Stream
Recorder --> App : None
deactivate Recorder
App --> Contributor : Show Stop / Recording; disable Play
deactivate App

note over Recorder, Stream
  Between button events, the audio callback copies incoming frames
  into recorder.frames while recording is true.
  Asynchronous callback messages are abstracted, not shown as blocking calls.
end note

Contributor -> App : toggle_recording() (Stop)
activate App
App -> Recorder : stop()
activate Recorder
note over Recorder : recording = false
Recorder -> Stream : stop() then close()
activate Stream
Stream --> Recorder : Stream stopped and closed
deactivate Stream
note over Recorder : stream = None;\nconcatenate captured frames, if any.
Recorder --> App : Audio array or None
deactivate Recorder
alt No frames / empty audio
  note over App : Show "No audio captured"; do not save a new file.
else Audio array contains samples
  App -> Audio : save_recording(audio, AUDIO_DIR)
  activate Audio
  note over Audio : sf.write(): UUID-named WAV at 44100 Hz.
  Audio --> App : Generated filename
  deactivate Audio
  note over App : Set pending_audio_path; enable Play.
end
App --> Contributor : Recording status displayed
deactivate App
deactivate Contributor
legend bottom
  Stream creation and synchronous calls have bounded activations.
  Staging a WAV does not append a dataset row: saving the form is separate.
  Library/device/write failures are not caught by these recording handlers.
endlegend
@enduml
